{
  "id": "ancestor-repair-selective",
  "name": "ancestor_repair_selective",
  "description": "Adopt only the ancestor-repair changes that demonstrably help. Pass 1 splices all 342 repaired rows over the shipped 5,012 and re-detects hierarchy consistency; diff_findings then isolates the rows whose flag actually cleared; pass 2 re-splices ONLY those, and the detectors run again on that deliverable. Motivated by the row-level diff of the full splice: 233 rows changed but only 138 cleared a flag, so 95 edits carried the intervention's regression risk (3 of 16 worsened on SME gold, e.g. 후복막 -> 후복강) with no measured upside. Baseline to beat: 580 rows flagged, 12 blockers, 4 contrast issues. Reads and re-promotes ko_imaging_deliverable, so the deliverable has an IDENTITY: a named, content-addressed object with a sha, rather than 'whichever selective splice ran most recently'. When SME feedback returns we can say which sha they reviewed.",
